# ============================================================================
# SAFETY RULE: no secret material may ever be committable by default.
# The key/wallet-shaped patterns below are deny-by-default — extend them
# freely, never narrow them. Real secrets live only in the encrypted vault.
# ============================================================================

# Build output
/target
# Standalone probe crates (probes/*) have their own target dirs; their
# Cargo.lock files ARE committed (reproducible probes) — only build output
# is ignored.
probes/*/target/
# cargo-fuzz (R10/F17/A23): the target is committed, the machine-generated
# corpora and crash artifacts are not. Q9 owns the minimized-corpus
# retention policy and will commit those deliberately, under its own path.
fuzz/target/
fuzz/corpus/
fuzz/artifacts/
fuzz/coverage/

# Devnet data (local Autonomi devnet + Anvil state; P16/P17)
devnet-data/
*.devnet/
# The P16 launcher's repo-local environment export (`scripts/devnet/local-up`):
# manifest + env file embed the funded Anvil dev key — a well-known public
# constant, but key-shaped material is never committable regardless.
# (`*.devnet/` above technically already matches `.devnet/` — `*` matches the
# empty string in gitignore globs — but the safety rule at the top of this
# file says deny-by-default patterns get stated explicitly, never inferred.)
.devnet/

# Wallet & key material
*.key
*.pem
wallets/
*wallet*.json
.secrets/

# ── Deny-by-default for the secret-shaped NAME families (Q263 / D161 §2 R9) ─
# The header rule above is the whole of the `private` class's enforcement:
# D161 §2 R2 adopts THIS FILE by reference as that class's register, so a
# family the patterns miss is a family nothing protects. Measured 2026-08-22
# with `git check-ignore -q` on names that create no files: `.env`,
# `.env.local`, `secrets.env`, `id_rsa` and `credentials.json` were NOT
# ignored — five of seven probes — while `foo.key` and `.secrets/a` were.
#
# THE BOUNDARY, so this block can be widened without swallowing the project:
# a name is denied here when the NAME ALONE means the content is credential
# material. `.env` qualifies. `.envrc` and `.npmrc` do NOT and are refused
# here on purpose — they are config files that MAY carry a token, and a token
# inside a file that is legitimately committed is `secret-guard`'s subject
# (Q2), which scans CONTENT over what is already staged. The two lines are
# complementary and neither substitutes for the other: this one stops the
# file being addable, that one stops a body slipping through a file that is.
#
# Patterns another pattern already covers are STATED ANYWAY, per the rule at
# `.devnet/` above — deny-by-default patterns are explicit, never inferred.
# Nothing here shadows a tracked path: `git ls-files -i -c --exclude-standard`
# measured 0 before this block and 0 after, so this is a PRESERVED invariant,
# not a repair. `scripts/ci-lanes.sh secret-guard` re-probes every family on
# every run and requires each verdict to come from THIS file, not from a
# developer's `.git/info/exclude` or a global excludes file.

# Environment files — the conventional home of API keys and RPC secrets.
.env
.env.*
*.env

# OpenSSH private keys: the basenames `ssh-keygen` writes, and the
# `<name>_<algo>` form a per-host or deploy key takes. The PUBLIC halves keep
# their `.pub` suffix and stay trackable ON PURPOSE — D71 §2 R5 publishes a
# minisign public key into this repository, and a rule that ate `.pub` would
# block the release act it exists to protect.
id_rsa
id_dsa
id_ecdsa
id_ecdsa_sk
id_ed25519
id_ed25519_sk
*_rsa
*_dsa
*_ecdsa
*_ecdsa_sk
*_ed25519
*_ed25519_sk
.ssh/

# Credential files whose NAME is the declaration: cloud/service-account JSON,
# the netrc pair, and git's own credential store — which holds
# `https://user:token@host` in cleartext.
credentials.json
*credentials*.json
.netrc
_netrc
.git-credentials

# Key and certificate containers. `*.key` and `*.pem` above cover the PEM
# flavours; these are the binary (PKCS#12) and PuTTY ones a TLS or EVM tool
# can emit.
*.p12
*.pfx
*.ppk

# Python bytecode. The repo carries dev tooling in scripts/ and
# testdata/vectors/v1/ (the cross-check checkers, the generators), and a
# `python3 scripts/…` run or an importlib load drops __pycache__ beside it.
# One such file reached a commit during the wave-7 freeze before this rule
# existed.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Editor droppings
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
.DS_Store

# Claude Code: committed agents live in .claude/agents/ — do NOT ignore
# .claude/ itself; only local settings stay out.
.claude/settings.local.json
# Agent worktrees are transient checkouts, never tracked
.claude/worktrees/
